type-scale (not in the standard): Type scale: readable sizes, no page zoom on fields, no duplicate roles, numeric weights. 7 findings.
  [decide] These font sizes are under 12 px. (2)
      Typography: font-size/label-xsmall (10 px)
      Typography: font-size/body-xsmall (10 px)
  [decide] These body roles are under 16 px. A form field's typed text uses a body role, and iOS zooms the page when a focused field's text is under 16 px. (Label roles are not counted: the zoom depends only on the field's own text.) (3)
      Typography: font-size/body-base (14 px)
      Typography: font-size/body-small (12 px)
      Typography: font-size/body-xsmall (10 px)
  [decide] These roles have identical font size and line height (16/24 px), so they are one style under several names. (3)
      Typography role heading-6
      Typography role label-large
      Typography role body-large
  [decide] These roles have identical font size and line height (14/20 px), so they are one style under several names. (3)
      Typography role section-label-base
      Typography role label-base
      Typography role body-base
  [decide] These roles have identical font size and line height (12/16 px), so they are one style under several names. (2)
      Typography role label-small
      Typography role body-small
  [decide] These roles have identical font size and line height (10/16 px), so they are one style under several names. (2)
      Typography role label-xsmall
      Typography role body-xsmall
  [decide] These weight tokens hold a style name instead of a number (CSS font-weight needs 100 to 900). (5)
      Typography: font-weight/heading (Bold)
      Typography: font-weight/section-label-base (Bold)
      Typography: font-weight/label (SemiBold)
      Typography: font-weight/body (Medium)
      Typography: font-weight/emphasis (Bold)

